		<title type="html"><![CDATA[Erreur pgfouine...]]></title>
		<link rel="alternate" href="http://forums.postgresql.fr/viewtopic.php?pid=12317#p12317"/>
		<content type="html"><![CDATA[<p>Bonjour à tous...<br />J&#039;ai l&#039;erreur suivante sur un appel à PGFOUINE : pgfouine.php -file /toto/pg_log/postgresql-05.log</p><p>$ pgfouine.php -file /var/akio/db/aic/pg_log/postgresql-05.log<br />pgFouine did not find any valid PostgreSQL log line in your log file:<br />* check that PostgreSQL uses an english locale for logging (lc_messages in your postgresql.conf),<br />* check that you use the -logtype option (syslog, stderr) according to your log file,<br />* if you use syslog and log_line_prefix, check that your log_line_prefix has a trailing space,<br />* if you use stderr, check that your log_line_prefix is of the form &#039;%t [%p]: [%l-1] &#039;.<br />If you think your log file and your options are correct, please contact the author (gsmet on #postgresql@freenode or guillaume-pg at smet dot org).<br />Ok !</p><br /><p>Voici un extrait de ma log <br />2012-01-05 13:00:09 CET [1844]: [5-1] LOG:&#160; durÃ©e : 0.175 ms<br />2012-01-05 13:05:56 CET [2301]: [1-1] LOG:&#160; durÃ©e : 55213.783 ms, instruction : ANALYZE;<br />OK !</p><br /><p>Voci mon postgres.conf :<br />log_destination = &#039;stderr&#039; <br />log_min_duration_statement = 5000<br />log_duration = on<br />et surtout<br />log_line_prefix = &#039;%t [%p]: [%l-1] &#039;...<br />OK </p><br /><p>Pourquoi cette erreur ? </p><p>Merci pour vos réponses..</p>]]></content>
